- This procedure can cause **trauma or pressure on surrounding structures**, including the **lateral femoral cutaneous nerve**, which runs through the retroperitoneum and can be compressed during IVC filter placement or due to hematoma formation.
- The **localized sensory loss** in the **lateral aspect of the thigh** is highly characteristic of **lateral femoral cutaneous nerve entrapment** (meralgia paresthetica).
- The **gradual improvement** of symptoms over a week supports a **mechanical or compressive etiology** rather than a progressive neurological condition like a stroke or hematoma.

